Statistical Analysis: Pre-Spring vs Post-Spring Performance (Cost-)
------------------------------------------------------------
Pre-spring sample size:  400
Post-spring sample size: 400
Pre-spring mean cost:    0.2434
Post-spring mean cost:   0.2387
------------------------------------------------------------
Result: The difference in costs is statistically insignificant.
Conclusion: The change in team decision-making did not result in a
            statistically significant shift in performance.

